rnment so  rather than  rather than playing these games  and giving cover to the dup for what is  essentially a wrecker's charter and  holding society to ransom the british  government could act constructively and  could be clear and could say to one and  all the issues in the protocol will be  resolved through the agreed mechanisms  and that boris johnson as prime minister  will lead and drive that effort and in  the meantime for the good of one and all  the executive needs to be formed by the  way the ulster unionist party's position  is that they are willing to enter in  executives just so as we're clear it is  one party the dup that is holding all  others to ransom at a time as michelle  has said when when people are facing  into a positive living crisis that we  haven't seen in 20 or 30 years and by  the way it's not going to get any easier  it's going to get much more difficult  that cost of living crisis into the  autumn and facing into the winter thank  you thanks folks  mcdonald and vice president michelle  o'neill they're addressing the assembled  press pack after their meeting with the  prime minister boris johnson it's just  been just over a week now since the  northern ireland election champaign the  largest party in the assembly ready uh  to form a power sharing government but  as they said they feel they are being  held to ransom by the dup and the  sticking point that northern ireland  protocol

